        "date": "2026-11-07T23:34:44Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(motion): the cross-drill station hop clears off-centre mouths\n\nThe hop plane between quarter-turn stations was sized for mouths on\ntheir stations' centre lines; an off-centre pair's chord could dip\ninside the bar (an (8,-6)/(-6,8) pair on r10 passed 10.757 mm from the\nspindle) and the rapid proof refused the op. traverse_s now measures\nthe chord between the two real hop points and raises the plane until\nit clears; on-centre pairs keep the closed-form plane exactly.\n\nFixes #81\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
